{"id": "EUVD-2026-82103", "enisaUuid": "5af44ba7-2e9d-3779-a9f3-16476bcc0df4", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\npinctrl: mediatek: use devm_gpiochip_add_data() for GPIO chip\n\nThe gpio_chip is allocated with device-managed memory but registered with\nthe non-managed gpiochip_add_data(). This was harmless while the drivers\nwere built-in, but once they can be built as modules and unbound/rmmod'd,\ndevm frees the gpio_chip's memory while it is still registered, causing a\nuse-after-free.\n\nRegister it with devm_gpiochip_add_data() so it shares the same\ndevice-managed lifecycle, which also lets the manual gpiochip_remove()\nerror paths go away.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:09:59", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:51:41", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dc6e5d802c88468290fee8826dd3a54cf58da25a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2490528a90a26f408ec3e95f865bad35454f9ff3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/01b5fcdc30c0ab35af960b60508eae1f7f7d32fd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b8fa1098ee9f627d38bdf7c0ef6c1a6058a4165b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9c650317ba553d297f3fc5f0ae40ec53d86f9dab"], "aliases": ["GHSA-6wqp-4g53-5h3x", "CVE-2026-92482"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "082cd5d5-df21-3132-ad3a-4a08425ef795", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "24da4dfe-1e74-3302-b3ef-e132f295ceea", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a6df410d420aa4ff316797d352f69e7ebae5ff98 <dc6e5d802c88468290fee8826dd3a54cf58da25a"}, {"id": "25191f7c-d320-3b4c-b4a9-65d558250913", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.1"}, {"id": "336afadf-546c-379f-ac14-f0c21d399fc8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a6df410d420aa4ff316797d352f69e7ebae5ff98 <01b5fcdc30c0ab35af960b60508eae1f7f7d32fd"}, {"id": "726b663c-1f98-3943-87bb-3bad7098a722", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "72d113ab-a1a0-358e-89ac-b71d51517212", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "a3560560-3e04-323e-99f5-965b972e4ac1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a6df410d420aa4ff316797d352f69e7ebae5ff98 <b8fa1098ee9f627d38bdf7c0ef6c1a6058a4165b"}, {"id": "cf34fb03-7981-3de9-9881-3820e183c636", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "d98f4def-7d50-34e6-a4fe-8948f4669de9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a6df410d420aa4ff316797d352f69e7ebae5ff98 <9c650317ba553d297f3fc5f0ae40ec53d86f9dab"}, {"id": "dc9f0fa5-3707-316a-b917-777bfd253369", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "ec596cff-3bab-399a-ae9b-1a9963f7268a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "f1bb4679-3900-3bbe-ac66-bc0151333f76", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a6df410d420aa4ff316797d352f69e7ebae5ff98 <2490528a90a26f408ec3e95f865bad35454f9ff3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "037c1e01-459d-377a-b3e2-240f9e6a620f", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}